cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VulnFC or build on this work, please cite the paper below."
type: software
title: "VulnFC — Truth under Input Poisoning Attacks: Benchmarking Fact-Checking Architectures"
abstract: >
  VulnFC is an input-poisoning vulnerability benchmark for fact-checking pipelines: victims are
  trained once on an unmodified corpus and the attack rewrites claims at evaluation time. It
  evaluates three victim families — recurrent networks (LSTM, Bi-LSTM, RNN), transformer SLMs under
  black-box and white-box access (BERT, RoBERTa), and locally served LLMs (Llama-3.2, Phi-3.5,
  Qwen-2.5) — against attack
  families spanning zero-cost prompt injection, semantic paraphrase, LLM-generated claims, Sybil
  flooding, and white-box FGSM/PGD, together with a variational truth-discovery defence (SSTF-VI).
  The release contains the evaluation code, the runner scripts, the result CSVs underlying every
  reported table. Attacks are scored against the label their rewrite leaves behind: a
  label-preserving rewrite against the original claim's label, a label-changing one against the
  rewritten claim's own.

# ICDE 2027 reviews single-blind, so authorship is disclosed at submission.
